    },
    {
      "id": "f02jgg0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Goods and Services Tax (GST)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kf5ug9p",
      "content": "• Introduced on 1 July 2017"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "snuxc2o",
      "content": "• Replaced many indirect taxes"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ennvqne",
      "content": "• Known as 'One Nation One Tax' reform"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "24h3pyb",
      "content": "• Types: CGST, SGST and IGST"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Article 112 covers the Annual Financial Statement (Union Budget) presented by the Finance Minister.",
        "Goods and Services Tax (GST) was introduced via the 101st Constitutional Amendment Act, 2016.",
        "Disinvestment receipts and recovery of loans are classified as Capital Receipts, not Revenue Receipts.",
        "Primary Deficit equals Fiscal Deficit minus net interest payments."
      ],
      "id": "8fgodu4"
    },
    {
      "id": "wskl6pn",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. Budget Deficit"
    },
    {
      "id": "35bf85z",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Deficit Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Meaning</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Fiscal Deficit</p>",
            "<p>Total expenditure minus total revenue</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Revenue Deficit</p>",
            "<p>Revenue expenditure minus revenue receipts</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Primary Deficit</p>",
            "<p>Fiscal deficit minus interest payments</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
